A poor loving couple each secretly sell their dearest treasure to buy a Christmas gift for the other, leaving both gifts unusable but proving their love the wisest of all.

1. Poor Love Two Treasures  (passages 1-2)
    Della and Jim are very poor but deeply in love, owning only two proud treasures, and Della
    is desperate to buy a worthy Christmas gift.
       -> Della has almost no money but desperately wants to give, so she must find another way
       to pay for a gift.
2. Della Sells Her Hair  (passages 3-3)
    Della cuts and sells her beautiful long hair to afford a fine platinum chain for Jim’s
    watch.
       -> With the new gift bought and her appearance changed, Della must go home and face Jim’s
       reaction.
3. Anxious Homecoming and Comfort  (passages 4-5)
    Della nervously waits for Jim, who is stunned by her short hair but says his love is
    unchanged before giving her a gift that moves her to tears.
       -> Jim’s mysterious gift package sets up the final reveal that he made an equal
       sacrifice.
4. Useless Gifts Wisest Love  (passages 6-6)
    Both gifts prove unusable because Jim sold his watch to buy combs for Della’s now-gone hair,
    yet their foolish sacrifices are celebrated as the wisest love.
